Subject: Add-transition store inline cache

What this does
  Add-transition store inline cache.

Why we need it
  `obj.x = v` on a fresh object (constructors, object literals) fell back to `JS_SetPropertyInternal2`, whose add path walks the shape/prototype chain and installs a transition; the store PIC only cached overwrites.

What it adds
  New `REG_PIC_ADD_W` kind in the site's secondary PIC way caches `pre-add shape -> post-add shape`; `regvm_put_field_ic` snapshots the pre-add shape (only when the secondary way is empty or already matches the receiver, so polymorphic sites do not thrash); `regvm_put_field_add_hit` replays the add (shape/extensible/non-exotic/prototype-epoch guard, grow, install shape, write slot); mirrored in the monolith and the regenerated step helpers, which also pick up the stale `sub_imm_s`/`sub_imm_self_s` float-overflow sign fix.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
